{"headword":"עָשַׁק","parent_lexicon":"BDB Dictionary","content":{"senses":[{"definition":"<strong>vb. oppress, wrong, extort (</strong>𝔗 <span dir=\"rtl\">עֲשַׁק</span> = BH, so Old Aramaic <span dir=\"rtl\">עשק</span>; Syriac <span dir=\"rtl\">ܥܫܰܩ</span> <em>accuse, slander;</em> Assyrian adj. <em>ešḳu</em>, <em>strong;</em> Arabic <span dir=\"rtl\">عَسَقٌ</span> <em>roughness, injustice</em><strong>)</strong>;—"},{"senses":[{"definition":"Pf. <span dir=\"rtl\">ע׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 5:21\" href=\"/Leviticus.5.21\">Lv 5:21</a>; <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 18:18\" href=\"/Ezekiel.18.18\">Ez 18:18</a>; 2 ms. sf. <span dir=\"rtl\">עֲשַׁקְתָּ֫נוּ</span> <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 12:4\" href=\"/I_Samuel.12.4\">1 S 12:4</a>, etc.; Impf. 3 ms. sf. <span dir=\"rtl\">יַעַשְׁקֻנִי</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 119:122\" href=\"/Psalms.119.122\">ψ 119:122</a>; 2 ms. <span dir=\"rtl\">תַּעֲשֹׁק</span> <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 19:13\" href=\"/Leviticus.19.13\">Lv 19:13</a> +, etc.; Inf. cstr. <span dir=\"rtl\">עֲשֹׁק</span> <a data-ref=\"Hosea 12:8\" href=\"/Hosea.12.8\">Ho 12:8</a>, sf. <span dir=\"rtl\">עָשְׁקָם</span> <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 16:21\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.16.21\">1 Ch 16:21</a> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 105:14\" href=\"/Psalms.105.14\">ψ 105:14</a>; <em>Pt.</em> act. <span dir=\"rtl\">עֹשֵׁק</span> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 14:31\" href=\"/Proverbs.14.31\">Pr 14:31</a> +, fpl. <span dir=\"rtl\">הָעשְׁקוֹת</span> <a data-ref=\"Amos 4:1\" href=\"/Amos.4.1\">Am 4:1</a>, etc.; pass. <span dir=\"rtl\">עָשׁוּק</span> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 28:29\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.28.29\">Dt 28:29</a> +, etc.;—"},{"senses":[{"definition":"<em>oppress, wrong</em> (often by extortion, ‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">גָּזַל</span>), c. acc. pers. <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 12:3\" href=\"/I_Samuel.12.3\">1 S 12:3</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 12:4\" href=\"/I_Samuel.12.4\">4</a> <a data-ref=\"Micah 2:2\" href=\"/Micah.2.2\">Mi 2:2</a> <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 5:21\" href=\"/Leviticus.5.21\">Lv 5:21</a>; <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 19:13\" href=\"/Leviticus.19.13\">19:13</a>; especially the poor and helpless <a data-ref=\"Amos 4:1\" href=\"/Amos.4.1\">Am 4:1</a> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 24:14\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.24.14\">Dt 24:14</a> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 7:6\" href=\"/Jeremiah.7.6\">Je 7:6</a> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 22:29\" href=\"/Ezekiel.22.29\">Ez 22:29</a> <a data-ref=\"Zechariah 7:10\" href=\"/Zechariah.7.10\">Zc 7:10</a> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 14:31\" href=\"/Proverbs.14.31\">Pr 14:31</a>; <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 22:16\" href=\"/Proverbs.22.16\">22:16</a>; <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 28:3\" href=\"/Proverbs.28.3\">28:3</a> <a data-ref=\"Ecclesiastes 4:1\" href=\"/Ecclesiastes.4.1\">Ec 4:1</a>; also c. acc. cogn. <span dir=\"rtl\">ע׳ עשֶׁק (וְ)גָזַל גָּזֵל</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 18:18\" href=\"/Ezekiel.18.18\">Ez 18:18</a> <em>practise extortion</em>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 22:29\" href=\"/Ezekiel.22.29\">22:29</a>, <em>take by extortion</em> <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 5:23\" href=\"/Leviticus.5.23\">Lv 5:23</a> and (c. acc. rei) <a data-ref=\"Malachi 3:5\" href=\"/Malachi.3.5\">Mal 3:5</a>; abs. <a data-ref=\"Hosea 12:8\" href=\"/Hosea.12.8\">Ho 12:8</a> <em>practise extortion;</em> <a data-ref=\"Job 10:3\" href=\"/Job.10.3\">Jb 10:3</a> <em>deal tyrannically</em> (of God); pt. <em>oppressor, extortioner</em> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 21:12\" href=\"/Jeremiah.21.12\">Je 21:12</a> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 72:4\" href=\"/Psalms.72.4\">ψ 72:4</a> <a data-ref=\"Ecclesiastes 4:1\" href=\"/Ecclesiastes.4.1\">Ec 4:1</a>; pt. pass. as subst. <em>the oppressed</em> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 103:6\" href=\"/Psalms.103.6\">ψ 103:6</a>; <a data-ref=\"Psalms 146:7\" href=\"/Psalms.146.7\">146:7</a>."}],"num":"1."},{"senses":[{"definition":"<em>oppress</em> a nation <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 52:4\" href=\"/Isaiah.52.4\">Is 52:4</a>, cf. <a data-ref=\"Psalms 105:14\" href=\"/Psalms.105.14\">ψ 105:14</a> = <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 16:21\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.16.21\">1 Ch 16:21</a>, <a data-ref=\"Psalms 119:122\" href=\"/Psalms.119.122\">ψ 119:122</a>, pt. act. <em>oppressor</em> v <a data-ref=\"Psalms 119:121\" href=\"/Psalms.119.121\">121</a>, pt. pass. <em>oppressed</em> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 50:33\" href=\"/Jeremiah.50.33\">Je 50:33</a>, in predict. <span dir=\"rtl\">ע׳ וְגָזוּל</span> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 28:29\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.28.29\">Dt 28:29</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">ע׳ וְרָצוּץ</span> v <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 28:33\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.28.33\">33</a> <a data-ref=\"Hosea 5:11\" href=\"/Hosea.5.11\">Ho 5:11</a>."}],"num":"2."},{"senses":[{"definition":"dub. are: <span dir=\"rtl\">יַעְשֹׁק נָהָר</span> <a data-ref=\"Job 40:23\" href=\"/Job.40.23\">Jb 40:23</a> <em>a river oppresses</em> him, i.e. rushes violently upon him (sc.; the hippopot.; Du <span dir=\"rtl\">יָשֹׁק</span>, from <span dir=\"rtl\">שׁוּק</span>; > Gunk Bu <span dir=\"rtl\">יִשְׁקַע</span> <em>fails, sinks</em>); <span dir=\"rtl\">עָשֻׁק בְּדַם נֶפֶשׁ</span> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 28:17\" href=\"/Proverbs.28.17\">Pr 28:17</a> <em>oppressed</em> (? <em>burdened</em>) with the blood of a person."}],"num":"3."}],"form":"Qal"},{"senses":[{"definition":"Pt. f. <span dir=\"rtl\">הַמְּעֻשָּׁקָה</span> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 23:12\" href=\"/Isaiah.23.12\">Is 23:12</a> <em>crushed</em> (of conquered Sidon under fig. of woman)."}],"form":"Pu."}]},"rid":"BDB07714","strong_numbers":["6231"],"next_hw":"עֹ֫שֶׁק","prev_hw":"עָשָׁן²","all_cited":true,"root":true,"quotes":[],"GK":["6943"],"TWOT":["1713"],"parent_lexicon_details":{"name":"BDB Dictionary","language":"heb.biblical","to_language":"eng","text_categories":[],"source":"BDB Dictionary","attribution":"F. Brown, S. Driver & C. Briggs","index_title":"BDB","version_title":"A Hebrew and English lexicon of the Old Testament, by Francis Brown. With the co-operation of S. R. Driver and Charles A. Briggs. Oxford, 1906","version_lang":"en","should_autocomplete":true}}